1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,604
Every year, trillions of dollars in goods travel across oceans, highways, and continents — connecting factories to shelves, and products to people.

2
00:00:11,684 --> 00:00:14,403
But what happens when that system breaks down?

3
00:00:14,403 --> 00:00:18,199
Supply chain disruptions are not just headlines.

4
00:00:18,255 --> 00:00:23,995
They are real events that ripple from a single delay into shortages felt around the world.

5
00:00:23,995 --> 00:00:34,745
Transportation delays — whether from port congestion, driver shortages, or severe weather — can hold products in limbo for weeks at a time.

6
00:00:34,745 --> 00:00:40,552
When a key supplier goes offline, the entire downstream chain grinds to a halt.

7
00:00:40,792 --> 00:00:46,155
A single missing component can stop production at facilities thousands of miles away.

8
00:00:46,155 --> 00:00:57,182
Global events — from pandemics to geopolitical conflicts to natural disasters — have shown us just how fragile interconnected supply chains can be.

9
00:00:57,182 --> 00:00:59,920
For businesses, the cost is immediate.

10
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:10,315
Inventory shortages mean lost sales, frustrated customers, and mounting pressure on operations teams scrambling to source alternatives.

11
00:01:10,315 --> 00:01:15,589
For consumers, it means empty shelves where your essentials should be.

12
00:01:15,738 --> 00:01:19,750
Longer lead times on the products you rely on every day.
